title ALES181 — Lotus's stereo_echo: the feedback delay carried into stereo, the SAME delay and feedback on BOTH channels, each channel reading and feeding back through its OWN live buffer — the first rung of the stereo TIME-BASED wing
prompt Autonomous loop lap after ALES180: recur through agent-doable work Lindy-first crux-first, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment to origin and xykj61 as its own signed round, STOP at custody gates.
think ALES176–180 carried the whole stereo MODULATION class (amplitude pair — tremolo, ring mod — beside the delay-line trio — vibrato, chorus, flanger). That class is now whole, so Lindy-first the next durable move OPENS a new stereo wing rather than accreting one more modulation. The echo (ALES66) is that wing's foundation: it opened the mono TIME-BASED wing with its primitive, the feedback delay y[i] = x[i] + fb·y[i-d], and chorus/flanger/reverb are each a delay line read a different way of it. Crux-first: the flanger (ALES180) already reads its own LIVE output through a feedback path, so the echo — the plain longer feedback delay the flanger's zero-depth case reduces to — is the base that whole wing stands on, and the SIMPLER live-feedback carry (a fixed whole delay, no LFO), the honest rung to seat a wing's foundation on.
think echo's three checks (BadDelay, BadFeedback, BadRange) were inline, so factored them into a shared pub precheck(clip_len, start, count, delay, fb_num, fb_den) mirroring ALES73's flanger refactor; mono ales-echo selftest re-ran GREEN (additive, reads a plain length so it touches no buffer). Composed stereo_echo mirroring the established pattern: StereoEchoError = echo.EchoError reused whole, validate ONCE against the shared length, then run echo.echo per channel with the SAME delay and feedback. Each channel reads and feeds back through its OWN live buffer — no cross-channel feedback, and because the delay is ≥ one whole sample buf[i-delay] sits strictly before the write index (an already-written output, dry audio, or silence), so an echo needs no carried state.
think Carried the flanger's honest panned-ratio limitation forward without re-hitting a RED: like the flanger and unlike the snapshot rungs, an accumulating feedback delay's @divTrunc truncation drifts an exact panned integer ratio by ones, so the image law proven is the identical-channel one (deterministic same-in→same-out, exact), stated plainly in doc, module header, GREEN string, and witness. The identical-channel law is the sense a mix cares about most (a centred voice stays centred).
think Proved three laws: stereo echo law (each channel == mono echo byte for byte with genuinely different per-channel content, the channels differing so no crossing); dry-identity law (fb_num=0 the exact dry master on both); image/balance/silence/atomicity/degenerate (an identical-channel master staying identical, silence to silence on both, left.len==right.len after, three refusals — BadDelay, BadFeedback, BadRange — each leaving both channels untouched and balanced, count 0 the identity).
obs No custody gate reached — pure local i16 DSP siloed to lotus/, a self-approved design round. Built and ran on metal; stereo_echo selftest GREEN directly and the witness GREEN through Rishi, TAME style bans clean. The stereo TIME-BASED wing now opens on its foundation, the plain feedback echo, ready for its own compositions (a real-time echo through the clock, a multitap, a stereo chorus/reverb) to climb next.
loom witness=ales_stereo_echo_witness selftest=GREEN laws=3 channels=2 wing=time-based-rung-1 refactor=echo-precheck-pub
